# ============================================================================
# WHAT SEIR-I SHOULD HAND TO SEIR-II
# ============================================================================
#
# SEIR-I should preserve trustworthy distinctions:
#
#
#       MODEL != SERVICE
#
#
#       SERVICE != DEPLOYMENT
#
#
#       DEPLOYMENT != ENDPOINT
#
#
#       ENDPOINT != PATH
#
#
#       ENDPOINT != HEALTH
#
#
#       ENDPOINT EXISTS != ENDPOINT READY
#
#
#       ENDPOINT READY != SERVICE HEALTHY
#
#
#       SERVICE HEALTHY != PATH REACHABLE
#
#
#       PATH REACHABLE != ROUTE AUTHORIZED
#
#
#       ROUTE AUTHORIZED != ROUTE SELECTED
#
#
# ============================================================================
# WHAT SEIR-II SHOULD NOT HAVE TO REPAIR
# ============================================================================
#
# SEIR-II should not discover that:
#
#
#       Kubernetes Service became AIService
#
#       Pod became AIModel
#
#       service_id became endpoint identity forever
#
#       Kubernetes became routing domain
#
#       cloud provider became AIRoute
#
#       K8s readiness became service health
#
#       endpoint presence became reachability
#
#       mTLS became AI authorization
#
#       labels became security policy
#
#       NetworkEndpointEvaluator became cluster-admin
#
#       EndpointSlice objects leaked into routing
#
#       endpoint.py swallowed health.py
#
#       endpoint.py swallowed path.py
#
#       Kubernetes SDK spread across Agent 11
#
#
# Those are exactly the mistakes this three-part design is trying to prevent.
#
#
# ============================================================================
# PART III DECISION RECORD
# ============================================================================
#
# CURRENT SEIR-I DECISION:
#
#
#       Endpoint behavior is infrastructure-neutral.
#
#
# CURRENT ABSTRACTION:
#
#
#       EndpointEvidenceSource
#
#
# CURRENT INITIAL IMPLEMENTATION:
#
#
#       StaticEndpointEvidenceSource
#
#
# EXPECTED NEAR-TERM IMPLEMENTATION:
#
#
#       KubernetesEndpointEvidenceSource
#
#
# CURRENT IoC RULE:
#
#
#       NetworkEndpointEvaluator receives the evidence source.
#
#
# CURRENT KUBERNETES IoC RULE:
#
#
#       Kubernetes adapter should receive its Kubernetes client
#       and mapping/configuration dependencies.
#
#
# CURRENT CORRELATION:
#
#
#       service_id
#
#
# CURRENT KNOWN LIMITATION:
#
#
#       service_id may eventually be too coarse for multi-deployment /
#       multi-cluster endpoint evidence.
#
#
# CURRENT NON-GOALS:
#
#
#       first-class NetworkEndpoint model
#
#       deployment model
#
#       cluster model
#
#       failure-domain model
#
#       health evaluation
#
#       path evaluation
#
#       policy evaluation
#
#       routing selection
#
#       Kubernetes remediation
#
#       multi-cluster aggregation
#
#       source reconciliation
#
#       endpoint telemetry model
#
#       endpoint history
#
#
# ============================================================================
# PART III FINAL INVARIANTS
# ============================================================================
#
#       FUTURE-AWARE != FUTURE-BLOATED
#
#
#       OPERATIONAL EVIDENCE
#           ->
#       DOMAIN REQUIREMENT
#           ->
#       CONTRACT
#           ->
#       BEHAVIOR
#
#
#       CURRENT CORRELATION KEY
#           !=
#       PERMANENT DOMAIN IDENTITY
#
#
#       MODEL != SERVICE != DEPLOYMENT != ENDPOINT
#
#
#       ENDPOINT != PATH
#
#       ENDPOINT != HEALTH
#
#
#       LOGICAL ENDPOINT != RESOLVED BACKEND
#
#
#       INFRASTRUCTURE COMPLEXITY
#           SHOULD BE TRANSLATED,
#       NOT REPLICATED
#
#
#       ROUTING DOMAIN
#           !=
#       CLOUD PROVIDER
